==Battleground==
*2 [[Tackey]]s spawn after 23.33 seconds<sup>700f</sup>, delay 4 seconds<sup>120f</sup>.
*1 [[Le'noir]] spawns after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>.
*1 [[Hackey]] spawns after 30 seconds<sup>900f</sup>.
*4 [[One Horn]]s spawn after 0.07 seconds<sup>2f</sup>, delay 3.33~4.67 seconds<sup>100f~140f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Ginger Snache]]s spawn after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>, delay 16.67~20 seconds<sup>500f~600f</sup>.
*4 [[One Horn]]s spawn after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>, delay 3.33~4.67 seconds<sup>100f~140f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This level is quite easy if you know what to do, since the One Horns stop spawning after a while. All you need to do is to kill the first ones with [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|A. Bahamut]], [[Apple Cat (Super Rare Cat)|iCat]] (in theory), [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]], and, basically, any short-ranged [[:Category:Anti-Red Cats|Anti-Red]] you have. [[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Jamiera Cats]] are great to help against the One Horns, as an attack and defense unit, but you have to always time your units well; [[Baby Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Cats in the Cradle]] is also incredibly good here.

When the One Horns die and only Le'noir, Hackey and Tackey remain, you just need to spam anyone who survives the hits of Le'noir (attention to Hackey) and there will be no way to lose (unless Hackey is hitting your base). In 4 crowns, use Courier Cat, then [[Flower Cat (Special Cat)|Bombercat]] with freeze [[Cat Combo|Combos]] for Le'noir.

Alternatively, if you have a [[Talents|Talented]] [[Dom Cat (Special Cat)|Dark Lazer]], boost her with Combos and let her take care of everything. She will use the One Horns as a stepping stone to kill the backliners.

==Trivia==
*Like most [[Singularityville]] stages, Virtual Harvest has a technology-related name - its Japanese name confirms that it refers to [[wikipedia:Virtual reality|virtual reality]] (VR).

